    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented in the `function/owner/*` classes. I've marked each as a **validation** (can reject) or a **side-effect** (mutates state).\n\n## Pre-pipeline gate\n\n0. **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`) \u2014 caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else the request is denied before any function runs.\n\n## Validations & normalizations (no transaction yet)\n\n1. **ValidateRequiredOwnerFields** \u2014 binds the body (no `@Valid`). Normalizes the **address** in place (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations), then requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` to be non-blank. Missing any \u2192 `MissingRequiredFieldsException` (**400**). Republishes the body.\n   - *Side-effect:* address rewritten to canonical form.\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 only if `postcode` present. Must be exactly 4 digits; and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must be in range. Unknown-region city accepts any 4 digits. Malformed/out-of-range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n\n3. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 only if `registrationDate` present. Must not be after the server's current date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n\n4. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 rewrites `telephone` to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+`/country code or assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits). Unconvertible \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 only if `email` present/non-blank: trims and lower-cases in place; must match the email regex and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com), else `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n\n## Transactional checks (governance `transaction` starts here, spanning through respond)\n\n6. **EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold: true`, the whole check is skipped. Otherwise scans all owners: rejects a **household duplicate** (same deterministic `householdId` = hash of canonical lastName + postcode) or a **contact duplicate** (same normalized telephone + email). Either \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n7. **EnsureCityBelowCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n8. **EnsureBelowDailyLimit** \u2014 rolls the effective registration date (supplied or today) forward to a business day, counts existing owners with that `registrationDate`; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## Side-effects (building and enriching the entity)\n\n9. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent; adjusts it forward onto a business day. Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n10. **AssignOwnerHousehold** \u2014 sets `householdId` = deterministic hash of (lastName, postcode). Runs for every owner.\n\n11. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash of normalized telephone + lastName).\n\n12. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing firstName+lastName (case-insensitive; excludes this new one).\n\n13. **CountHouseholdMembers** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the same `householdId` + 1 (this owner).\n\n14. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 a `sharesHousehold` owner is never flagged (sets flag false / of null). Otherwise, if it shares an existing owner's lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the lowest matching owner id; else false/null.\n\n15. **SaveOwner** \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n16. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line with the new id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`.\n\n17. **EvaluateBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets the transient `bulkSignupWarning=true` when > 80 owners share this owner's business-day `registrationDate` (this one now saved/counted); else false.\n\n18. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Notes on ordering semantics:** required-field/postcode/date checks come *before* telephone/email normalization, so those 400s fire on raw input; all three duplicate/capacity/limit checks and every mutating step share one `transaction`, so the whole thing commits once at `respond` (any escalation rolls it back). The uniqueness, capacity, daily-limit, namesake, household-size, soft-duplicate, and bulk-signup steps each independently scan `ownerRepository.findAll()`."
